A||||5||maryjane||uneven idle code 44||||1||
Z||000000||maryjane||07-22-2001||10:18 AM||||last night the car wouldn't start, I mean wouldn't turn over. Dash indicators came on till key is turned to start, then everything goes dead. Traced the trouble to corrosion on positive batt cable this morning. Took it off, cleaned it up and reinstalled it. Took forever to idle down to 1000, idles rough and no accel on the road. eng light came on briefly and went off. codes checked-returned 44-lean exh. checked for vac leaks,couldn't find any.Plan to change oxy sensor, it's never been changed in the 4 yrs we've had it.<BR>Is it just a coincidence it failed or could it be caused by the bad batt connection? thanks,<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||07-22-2001||10:23 AM||||Don,<P>It could be related to the battery connection, Especially if the ECM lost power and cleared memory. The IAC is searching for reset data, if you can take it out on the road and drive around over 35 mph or faster for a while.<BR>I had replaced the IAC in one of my '86's yesterday and it refused to reset until I took the car down the interstate at 90+ for 1.5 miles. Did fine after that!<BR>Worth a shot.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||07-22-2001||11:24 AM||||All true.  When you remove power from the ECM it will automatically reset and remain in open loop mode until the car has warmed up and was driven at least 35MPH.  At that point the ECM *should* reset and resume normal operation.<P>Until you've done that you should be suspicious of the validity of a code 44.   <P>If you're lucky enough to have an Auto X-ray  or == you can use it to monitor the reported voltage from the O2 sensor; if they're near 0 millivolts the sensor has failed (and you should see code 44s) and needs to be replaced. The ECM tries to regulate emissions so that the O2 sensor reports values bouncing above and below 450 millivolts. <P>A bad O2 sensor can cause rough idle or an idle that oscillates +/- 200-300 RPM every 1-2 seconds.  <P>If you've never changed one, on a V6 it's straightforward and should take you way less than 30 minutes to do.  If the exhaust is hot you do risk burning your hands or arms. Space is pretty tight so I use a 7/8 crowsfoot wrench. <P>IMO on the 2.8L its easier to remove and replace the sensor itself from above the engine but way easier to disconnect and reconnect the cable by putting the rear of the car on jackstands and getting underneath.<P>For the 2.8L the Delco p/n is 25162693, list price is $52.  Don't bother with any of the 3rd party ones.   ||||reg||14
Z||000003||maryjane||07-22-2001||11:27 AM||||Thanks,I did drive it but not over 40mph and only a couple miles. Didn't want to get stranded in the boonies.I disconnected the - bat cable to clear old codes, after startup, eng light came on again briefly and #44 was set again.<BR>When exh cools off, I'll go ahead and chng O2 sensor. Are Bosch components any good? Only thing I could get on short notice.<BR>LarryB, you must have posted while I was writing this, you answered my question about the Bosch. Thanks<BR>Don<BR>edited to acknowledge LarryB's reply.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||07-22-2001||12:45 PM||||Well..... Consider that Bosch is usually credited with inventing the O2 sensor...<P>They are the only ones I'll use. Second choice is to use ACdelco for GM, Motorcraft for Ford and so on.<P>I've seen odd problems show up from some off branded O2 sensors. Batty O2 sensors often cause problems w/o setting codes. It's just not worth the trouble to mess with off brands for that one. It's not like some other sensors where only one or two companies actually made it no matter who's name is on the box.||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||07-22-2001||09:58 PM||||Update: I went ahead & changed O2.4yrs old, it's time. Still ran like crap, eng light on. Took out on the loop(yeah we got paved roads in Texas), coaxed it up to 45 and up. When it hit 55, it kicked in & eng light went off. Drove at 70 (spd limit) for a few miles, been fine ever since. Thanks guys,man I love this place.<BR>Don||||reg||1
